second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"Inquiry about the residence would be: \\\"Where does Leopold Haftel reside?\\\"\", \"slot_hint\": \"other\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 72, \"text\": \"Title: The Unbroken Spirit of Leopold Haftel: A Holocaust Victim's Story\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 74, \"end\": 235, \"text\": \"In the heart of the Czech Republic, where the River Svratka flows gently through the city, lies Brno, a statutory city with a rich history and cultural heritage.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 236, \"end\": 423, \"text\": \"It is here, in this vibrant city, that our story begins, a story of resilience, hope, and tragedy, centered around the life of Leopold Haftel, a Holocaust victim born on February 2, 1859.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 424, \"end\": 502, \"text\": \"Leopold's early life in Brno was marked by a sense of community and belonging.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 503, \"end\": 652, \"text\": \"As a young man, he was an integral part of the city's thriving Jewish population, which had been an essential fabric of Brno's society for centuries.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 653, \"end\": 796, \"text\": \"The Haftel family, with their roots in the city dating back to the 18th century, was well-respected and known for their entrepreneurial spirit.\"}, \"D1S7\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 797, \"end\": 943, \"text\": \"Leopold's father, a successful merchant, had built a prosperous business, providing for his family and contributing to the city's economic growth.\"}, \"D1S8\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 944, \"end\": 1070, \"text\": \"As Leopold grew older, he became increasingly involved in the family business, learning the intricacies of trade and commerce.\"}, \"D1S9\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1071, \"end\": 1186, \"text\": \"His natural aptitude for numbers and his keen business sense made him an invaluable asset to the family enterprise.\"}, \"D1S10\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1187, \"end\": 1339, \"text\": \"The Haftels were a prominent fixture in Brno's commercial circles, and Leopold's reputation as a shrewd and fair businessman spread throughout the city.\"}, \"D1S11\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1340, \"end\": 1468, \"text\": \"However, the winds of change were blowing across Europe, and the Haftel family's fortunes were about to take a devastating turn.\"}, \"D1S12\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1469, \"end\": 1607, \"text\": \"The rise of Nazi Germany and its aggressive expansion into Czechoslovakia in 1939 marked the beginning of a dark period in Brno's history.\"}, \"D1S13\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1608, \"end\": 1712, \"text\": \"The city, once a beacon of tolerance and coexistence, was soon engulfed in the horrors of the Holocaust.\"}, \"D1S14\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1713, \"end\": 1814, \"text\": \"Leopold, now in his early eighties, was forced to confront the brutal reality of the Nazi occupation.\"}, \"D1S15\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1815, \"end\": 1902, \"text\": \"His business, built over decades, was seized, and his family's assets were confiscated.\"}, \"D1S16\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1903, \"end\": 2034, \"text\": \"The once-thriving Jewish community of Brno was systematically dismantled, with many of its members deported to concentration camps.\"}, \"D1S17\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 2035, \"end\": 2106, \"text\": \"Despite the unimaginable hardships, Leopold's spirit remained unbroken.\"}, \"D1S18\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 2107, \"end\": 2211, \"text\": \"He continued to reside in Brno, a testament to his resilience and determination to hold on to his roots.\"}, \"D1S19\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 2212, \"end\": 2345, \"text\": \"The city, which had been his home for over eight decades, was now a constant reminder of the tragedy that had befallen his community.\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 151, \"text\": \"As the last wisps of winter's chill dissipated, Leopold Haftel emerged from the cozy confines of his Loppi cottage, breathing in the crisp Finnish air.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 152, \"end\": 250, \"text\": \"The scent of freshly baked rye bread wafted from the nearby bakery, enticing him to start his day.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 251, \"end\": 356, \"text\": \"He donned his worn fedora, its brim creased from years of use, and set out to tend to his beloved garden.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 357, \"end\": 536, \"text\": \"The villagers, familiar with Leopold's gentle nature and remarkable green thumb, would often remark on the vibrant blooms that seemed to burst forth from the earth under his care.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 537, \"end\": 698, \"text\": \"Today, he intended to coax his prized roses into bloom, their delicate petals a reminder of the beauty that still existed in a world that had once been so cruel.\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 699, \"end\": 796, \"text\": \"As he worked the soil, Leopold's mind wandered back to the memories he had tried to leave behind.\"}, \"D2S7\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 797, \"end\": 892, \"text\": \"The horrors of the war, the loss of loved ones, and the scars that still lingered on his heart.\"}, \"D2S8\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 893, \"end\": 927, \"text\": \"But in Loppi, he had found solace.\"}, \"D2S9\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 928, \"end\": 1032, \"text\": \"The quiet, rolling hills and the kindness of the people had slowly begun to heal the wounds of his past.\"}, \"D2S10\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1033, \"end\": 1085, \"text\": \"A soft voice interrupted his reverie, \\\"Hei, Leopold!\"}, \"D2S11\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1086, \"end\": 1108, \"text\": \"Onko kaikki kunnossa?\\\"\"}, \"D2S12\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1109, \"end\": 1199, \"text\": \"It was Aino, the baker's daughter, come to deliver a fresh loaf and exchange pleasantries.\"}, \"D2S13\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1200, \"end\": 1303, \"text\": \"Leopold smiled, his eyes crinkling at the corners, as he replied in his halting Finnish, \\\"Kiitos, Aino.\"}, \"D2S14\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1304, \"end\": 1321, \"text\": \"Kaikki on hyvää.\\\"\"}, \"D2S15\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1322, \"end\": 1412, \"text\": \"The gentle exchange was a small but significant reminder that, here in Loppi, he was home.\"}, \"D2S16\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1413, \"end\": 1544, \"text\": \"As the sun climbed higher in the sky, Leopold returned to his cottage, his hands stained with earth and his heart a little lighter.\"}, \"D2S17\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1545, \"end\": 1689, \"text\": \"He settled into his favorite armchair, surrounded by the memories of a life rebuilt, and began to read from the worn pages of his favorite book.\"}, \"D2S18\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1690, \"end\": 1791, \"text\": \"The words blurred together as his eyes grew heavy, lulled by the peacefulness of his adopted village.\"}, \"D2S19\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1792, \"end\": 1893, \"text\": \"In this quiet, idyllic scene, it was easy to forget the turmoil that had once defined Leopold's life.\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"card_id\": \"d1:c0\", \"entity\": \"Leopold Haftel\", \"scope\": \"residence\", \"claim\": \"Leopold Haftel continued to reside in Brno despite the Nazi occupation.\", \"answer\": \"Brno\", \"quote\": \"He continued to reside in Brno, a testament to his resilience and determination to hold on to his roots.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"card_id\": \"d2:c0\", \"entity\": \"Leopold Haftel\", \"scope\": \"residence\", \"claim\": \"Leopold Haftel resides in Loppi.\", \"answer\": \"Loppi\", \"quote\": \"As the last wisps of winter's chill dissipated, Leopold Haftel emerged from the cozy confines of his Loppi cottage, breathing in the crisp Finnish air. The scent of freshly baked rye bread wafted from the nearby bakery, enticing him to start his day. He donned his worn fedora, its brim creased from years of use, and set out to tend to his beloved garden. The villagers, familiar with Leopold's gentle nature and remarkable green thumb, would often remark on the vibrant blooms that seemed to burst forth from the earth under his care. Today, he intended to coax his prized roses into bloom, their delicate petals a reminder of the beauty that still existed in a world that had once been so cruel. As he worked the soil, Leopold's mind wandered back to the memories he had tried to leave behind. The horrors of the war, the loss of loved ones, and the scars that still lingered on his heart. But in Loppi, he had found solace. The quiet, rolling hills and the kindness of the people had slowly begun to heal the wounds of his past. A soft voice interrupted his reverie, \\\"Hei, Leopold! Onko kaikki kunnossa?\\\" It was Aino, the baker's daughter, come to deliver a fresh loaf and exchange pleasantries. Leopold smiled, his eyes crinkling at the corners, as he replied in his halting Finnish, \\\"Kiitos, Aino. Kaikki on hyvää.\\\" The gentle exchange was a small but significant reminder that, here in Loppi, he was home.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}], \"R5_answers\": [\"Brno\", \"Loppi\"], \"candidates\": [{\"id\": \"C0\", \"answer\": \"Brno\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C1\", \"answer\": \"Loppi\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}]}"
